@matchai I get it that you want a single, simple, cross-platform file location but the thing is the current location `~/.config/starship.toml` is just... wrong.

`~/.config/starship/config.toml` has all the qualities that you require, with the added benefit of it being a standard. You did exactly this with the cache location `~/.cache/starship/session_XYZ.log`. So there's a discrepancy within starship's usage of file locations itself, let alone standard locations.

Also, support for `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` will _not_ introduce a new config file location, rather a way to **override** it, similar to `STARSHIP_CONFIG`. The difference is that the latter overrides the config _file_ location, while the former overrides the config _directory_ location. Therefore one's existence doesn't eliminate the need for the other, they serve different purposes.

Same applies to `XDG_CACHE_HOME` (BTW see [#7092](https://github.com/starship/starship/pull/7092)).

